EMPLOYEE DISCIPLINE PROCESS.

00:33:00.178 --> 00:33:01.212
TURNING BRIEFLY TO THE JANUARY

00:33:01.279 --> 00:33:03.514
SPECIAL REPORT IN JULY OF LAST

00:33:03.581 --> 00:33:04.649
YEAR, DURING THE COURSE OF OUR

00:33:04.716 --> 00:33:07.618
MONITORING, WE RECEIVED A CDCR

00:33:07.685 --> 00:33:10.888
MEMORANDUM OUTLINING A DIRECTIVE

00:33:10.955 --> 00:33:11.889
TO CONVERT BACKLOG GRIEVANCES

00:33:11.956 --> 00:33:13.191
CONTAINING ALLEGATIONS OF STAFF

00:33:13.257 --> 00:33:14.325
MISCONDUCT THAT SHOULD HAVE BEEN

00:33:14.392 --> 00:33:17.061
INVESTIGATED BY THE OFFICE OF

00:33:17.128 --> 00:33:18.129
INTERNAL AFFAIRS INTO ROUTINE

00:33:18.196 --> 00:33:20.465
GRIEVANCES THAT WOULD BE

00:33:20.531 --> 00:33:22.233
ADDRESSED BY LOCAL PRISON STAFF.

00:33:22.300 --> 00:33:23.634
INSTEAD THE DIRECTIVE APPEARED

00:33:23.701 --> 00:33:24.635
TO VIOLATE CDCR'S NEW

00:33:24.702 --> 00:33:26.771
REGULATIONS, SO WE IMMEDIATELY

00:33:26.838 --> 00:33:28.439
BEGAN LOOKING INTO IT. WE

00:33:28.506 --> 00:33:30.375
LEARNED THAT BEGINNING IN

00:33:30.441 --> 00:33:33.244
FEBRUARY OF 2022, CDCR BEGAN

00:33:33.311 --> 00:33:37.115
DEVELOPING A BACKLOG OF OVER 900

00:33:37.181 --> 00:33:38.249
GRIEVANCES THAT THE CENTRALIZED

00:33:38.316 --> 00:33:39.851
SCREENING TEAM IDENTIFIED AS

00:33:39.917 --> 00:33:40.885
CONTAINING ALLEGATIONS OF STAFF

00:33:40.952 --> 00:33:43.454
MISCONDUCT. THE GRIEVANCES THAT

00:33:43.521 --> 00:33:45.223
HAD BEEN REFERRED TO THE OFFICE

00:33:45.289 --> 00:33:46.824
OF INTERNAL AFFAIRS FOR AN

00:33:46.891 --> 00:33:47.759
ALLEGATION, INQUIRY OR

00:33:47.825 --> 00:33:49.026
INVESTIGATION HAD NOT YET BEEN

00:33:49.093 --> 00:33:52.897
PROCESSED. AS A RESULT OF THE

00:33:52.964 --> 00:33:55.133
DIRECTIVE, CDCR WOUND UP CLOSING

00:33:55.199 --> 00:33:58.870
595 CASES CONTAINING ALLEGATIONS

00:33:58.936 --> 00:33:59.303
OF STAFF MISCONDUCT,

00:33:59.370 --> 00:34:02.006
RECLASSIFYING THEM AS ROUTINE

00:34:02.073 --> 00:34:03.007
GRIEVANCES AND REDIRECTING THEM

00:34:03.074 --> 00:34:05.576
TO THE PRISON GRIEVANCE OFFICES

00:34:05.643 --> 00:34:06.778
TO BE OPENED AS NEW ROUTINE

00:34:06.844 --> 00:34:09.046
GRIEVANCES. BEING MINDFUL OF

00:34:09.113 --> 00:34:10.748
TIME, I WILL QUICKLY HIGHLIGHT

00:34:10.815 --> 00:34:13.050
SOME OF OUR FINDINGS. FIRST WAS

00:34:13.117 --> 00:34:15.853
THAT CDCR ALLOWED THE STATUTE OF

00:34:15.920 --> 00:34:16.954
LIMITATIONS TO TAKE DISCIPLINARY

00:34:17.021 --> 00:34:20.425
ACTION TO EXPIRE IN MANY OF THE

00:34:20.491 --> 00:34:21.426
GRIEVANCES BEFORE THEY WERE

00:34:21.492 --> 00:34:23.060
REDIRECTED, STATE LAW GENERALLY

00:34:23.127 --> 00:34:24.162
REQUIRES THAT DISCIPLINE AGAINST

00:34:24.228 --> 00:34:27.031
PEACE OFFICERS OCCUR WITHIN ONE

00:34:27.098 --> 00:34:28.833
YEAR OF DISCOVERY OF THE ALLEGED

00:34:28.900 --> 00:34:30.768
MISCONDUCT IN THREE YEARS FOR

00:34:30.835 --> 00:34:31.969
ALL OTHER STAFF, WE FOUND THAT

00:34:32.036 --> 00:34:33.905
THE STATUTE OF LIMITATIONS

00:34:33.971 --> 00:34:36.741
EXPIRED IN 127 OF THOSE CASES

00:34:36.808 --> 00:34:37.742
BEFORE CDCR EVEN BEGAN

00:34:37.809 --> 00:34:40.211
REDIRECTING THEM BACK TO THE

00:34:40.278 --> 00:34:43.281
PRISONS. AS A RESULT, CDCR WAS

00:34:43.347 --> 00:34:44.348
POWERLESS TO DISCIPLINE STAFF IF

00:34:44.415 --> 00:34:45.716
ALLEGATIONS OF STAFF MISCONDUCT

00:34:45.783 --> 00:34:47.652
WERE FOUND TO HAVE OCCURRED. 129

00:34:47.718 --> 00:34:50.855
OF THE GRIEVANCES WERE SENT BACK

00:34:50.922 --> 00:34:52.056
WITHIN 60 DAYS OF THE STATUTE

00:34:52.123 --> 00:34:53.491
EXPIRING, WHICH GIVES THE

00:34:53.558 --> 00:34:54.625
DEPARTMENT A VERY SHORT TIME TO

00:34:54.692 --> 00:34:55.660
REVIEW, INVESTIGATE AND HOLD

00:34:55.726 --> 00:34:58.396
STAFF ACCOUNTABLE. WE ALSO FOUND

00:34:58.463 --> 00:35:02.033
THAT A SECOND FINDING WAS IN 71

00:35:02.099 --> 00:35:05.236
OF THE 595 GRIEVANCES. CDCR

00:35:05.303 --> 00:35:08.873
CLOSED AND RECLASSIFIED THEM AS

00:35:08.940 --> 00:35:10.041
ROUTINE, AND WE FOUND THAT IN

00:35:10.107 --> 00:35:12.109
EACH OF THOSE, AT LEAST ONE,

00:35:12.176 --> 00:35:13.244
THERE WAS ONE ALLEGATION OF

00:35:13.311 --> 00:35:16.347
STAFF MISCONDUCT AND STAFF

00:35:16.414 --> 00:35:17.381
MISCONDUCT, WHICH WOULD REQUIRE

00:35:17.448 --> 00:35:19.016
A COMPLEX ISSUE REQUIRING

00:35:19.083 --> 00:35:21.986
SPECIALIZED INVESTIGATIVE SKILLS

00:35:22.053 --> 00:35:23.054
TO BE INVESTIGATED, SUCH AS

00:35:23.120 --> 00:35:25.156
RETALIATION, DISCRIMINATION, AND

00:35:25.223 --> 00:35:26.257
DISHONESTY. THESE ARE THE TYPES

00:35:26.324 --> 00:35:29.527
OF ALLEGATIONS THAT ARE REQUIRED

00:35:29.594 --> 00:35:31.395
TO BE REFERRED TO THE OFFICE OF

00:35:31.462 --> 00:35:34.932
INTERNAL AFFAIRS. ALLEGATIONS

00:35:34.999 --> 00:35:36.667
INVESTIGATION UNIT. WE FOUND

00:35:36.734 --> 00:35:37.902
THAT AT LEAST 16 OF THOSE 71

00:35:37.969 --> 00:35:39.470
CASES WERE NOT WERE NOT EVEN

00:35:39.537 --> 00:35:40.371
INVESTIGATED BY LOCALLY

00:35:40.438 --> 00:35:42.874
DESIGNATED INVESTIGATORS, WHO

00:35:42.940 --> 00:35:44.075
MOST LIKELY DID NOT RECEIVE THAT

00:35:44.141 --> 00:35:45.142
SPECIALIZED SKILL IN CONDUCTING

00:35:45.209 --> 00:35:47.945
THOSE INVESTIGATIONS. A THIRD

00:35:48.012 --> 00:35:49.814
FINDING WAS THAT WE FOUND THAT

00:35:49.881 --> 00:35:50.748
THESE CASES WERE NOT BEING,

00:35:50.815 --> 00:35:55.620
TIMELY INVESTIGATED. REGULATIONS

00:35:55.686 --> 00:35:57.221
. GENERALLY REQUIRE THAT THESE

00:35:57.288 --> 00:35:58.456
ALLEGATIONS BE COMPLETED WITHIN

